## 4. User Interface Design
### 4.1 Design Style
- Primary colors: Industrial blue (#165DFF) for trust/reliability, safety orange (#FF7D00) for alerts
- Secondary colors: Neutral grays for content, green (#00B42A) for status completions
- Button style: Rounded corners (8px), elevated cards with subtle shadows
- Font: Inter family, 14px base size, 16px for interactive elements
- Layout: Bottom navigation for mobile, top navigation with map overlay for navigation views
- Icons: Material Design icons consistent with logistics/transport use cases

### 4.2 Page Design Overview
| Page Name | Module Name | UI Elements |
|-----------|-------------|-------------|
| Home Dashboard | Status Tracker | Large status pill showing current trip state, countdown timer for delivery window, map snippet of current route |
| Scanning Page | Camera View | Full-screen camera interface with scan frame, flash toggle, manual entry fallback, connection status indicator for offline mode |
| POD Page | Verification Options | Three card-based options for PIN, photo, signature; large touch targets for on-site use; progress indicator showing POD completion |
| Earnings Page | Summary Cards | Color-coded cards for approved/pending income, red alert badges for unapproved expenses, transaction list with filter chips |

### 4.3 Responsiveness
Mobile-first design optimized for smartphones and tablets used in field conditions. Touch interactions optimized for gloved operation where applicable. Offline mode maintains full functionality without connectivity.

### 4.4 Location & Mapping Requirements
- Google Maps SDK integration with offline map caching
- Geofence radius visualization on map (100m circle around delivery address)
- Real-time location tracking with 5-second update interval
- Route recalculation with traffic avoidance
- Dark mode support for low-light operations
